<%- include('partials/header', { title: 'API Documentation', user: user }) %>
<div class="row">
  <div class="col-12">
    <h2>API Documentation</h2>
    <p>This application exposes REST APIs for authentication and employee management. Use the API to log in, read employee data, and manage employees with admin permissions.</p>

    <h3>1. POST /api/login</h3>
    <p>Authenticate a user and receive a JWT token.</p>
    <pre><code>{
  "username": "admin",
  "password": "Password123"
}</code></pre>
    <p>Response:</p>
    <pre><code>{
  "token": "...",
  "user": {
    "id": 1,
    "username": "admin",
    "role": "admin"
  }
}</code></pre>

    <h3>2. GET /api/employees</h3>
    <p>Get paginated employee records. Requires `Authorization: Bearer &lt;token&gt;`.</p>
    <p>Query parameters:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><code>page</code> - page number (default 1)</li>
      <li><code>q</code> - search by full name or email</li>
      <li><code>sort</code> - <code>name</code> or <code>joining_date</code></li>
      <li><code>dir</code> - <code>asc</code> or <code>desc</code></li>
    </ul>
    <pre><code>{
  "total": 4,
  "page": 1,
  "pageSize": 10,
  "employees": [ ... ]
}</code></pre>

    <h3>3. GET /api/employees/:id</h3>
    <p>Get a single employee by ID. Requires JWT authorization.</p>
    <pre><code>{
  "id": 1,
  "employee_code": "EMP-0001",
  "full_name": "Priya Sharma",
  "email": "priya.sharma@example.com",
  "mobile": "9876543210",
  "department_id": 1,
  "designation": "Software Engineer",
  "salary": 65000,
  "joining_date": "2024-01-15",
  "status": "Active"
}</code></pre>

    <h3>4. POST /api/employees</h3>
    <p>Create a new employee. Requires admin role and JWT authorization.</p>
    <pre><code>{
  "full_name": "New Employee",
  "email": "new.employee@example.com",
  "mobile": "9876543219",
  "department_id": 1,
  "designation": "Developer",
  "salary": 50000,
  "joining_date": "2025-01-01",
  "status": "Active"
}</code></pre>

    <h3>5. PUT /api/employees/:id</h3>
    <p>Update an employee's details. Requires admin role and JWT authorization.</p>
    <pre><code>{
  "full_name": "Updated Name",
  "email": "updated.email@example.com",
  "mobile": "9876543219",
  "department_id": 2,
  "designation": "Senior Developer",
  "salary": 70000,
  "joining_date": "2024-05-01",
  "status": "Active"
}</code></pre>

    <h3>6. DELETE /api/employees/:id</h3>
    <p>Soft delete an employee by ID. Requires admin role and JWT authorization.</p>
    <pre><code>{ "message": "Employee deleted successfully." }</code></pre>

    <h3>Request Headers</h3>
    <pre><code>Authorization: Bearer &lt;token&gt;
Content-Type: application/json</code></pre>

    <h3>Notes</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Email must be unique.</li>
      <li>Mobile number must be exactly 10 digits.</li>
      <li>Salary must be greater than 0.</li>
      <li>Employee code is auto-generated by the system.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</div>
